SI bug pattern (drives migration): backend now emits explicit-SI fields
(total_distance_km, range_km, avg_efficiency_wh_km, speed_stats.max km/h,
totalDistanceKm, avgEfficiencyWhKm, avgSpeedKmh, topSpeedKmh). Legacy
useSettings.convertDistance/convertSpeed/convertEfficiency expects
miles/mph/Wh-per-mile inputs and silently mis-renders for both unit prefs.
Same root-cause Phase-43/0023 fixed in BatteryDegradationPage.

useUnits + convertXFromSI boundary helpers from @/lib/unitConversion are
the locked-policy replacement. No SI helper exists for Wh/km display so an
inline KM_PER_MILE = 1.609344 multiplicand is used (whPerKm * 1.609344 =
Wh/mi for unit_of_length=mi users; identity for km).

