=== NOTES ===
1. Same SI-bug pattern Phase-43/0023 fixed in BatteryDegradationPage and
   Phase-43/0022 fixed in features/driving — applied here to 18 files.
2. Wh/km efficiency conversion uses an inline KM_PER_MILE = 1.609344 factor
   because @/lib/unitConversion exposes no convertEfficiencyFromSI helper.
   Future cleanup: introduce convertEnergyPerDistanceFromSI(whPerKm, prefs).
3. PeriodComparePage's pctChange call sites retain RAW SI values because
   percentage change is unit-invariant under linear conversion (% is the
   same whether you compute distA/distB in km or mi).
4. StatisticsPage stateSummary reduce() now reads both totalMin AND
   total_min via dual-key fallback so any future replacement endpoint
   emitting snake_case will work without a follow-up edit. camelCaseKeys
   already retains both keys at runtime (resilience.ts:19-34).
5. FleetComparePage retained useSettings for fmtDistance / fmtTemp /
   currencySymbol — these have no SI replacement and are unaffected by
   the km vs mi bug.
6. MileagePage / TimelinePage hooks return 404 today (deleted endpoints)
   but the migration is applied anyway so the page is bug-free when a
   replacement lands. The deprecated hooks themselves are flagged via
   @deprecated JSDoc.
7. WeeklyDigestPage was DEFERRED — its in-tree useWeeklyDigest reads a
   Drive type whose fields don't exist on the new backend Drive
   (distance / start_date / efficiency_wh_km vs distance_mi / start_ts /
   energy_used_kwh). Pre-existing runtime bug requiring a separate
   backend-shape audit out of scope here.
8. Gate workarounds applied (matches prior phase precedents):
   - .\node_modules\.bin\tsc.cmd + npm.cmd run build instead of npx /
     bare-npm because pwsh -File invocation triggers npm 10's
     "could not determine executable to run" error.
   - Audit grep written via temp script + Remove-Item self-delete to
     avoid here-string parser bugs ("$f:" was interpreted as a variable
     scope in the original inline form on PowerShell 7); changed to
     ('{0}: tag' -f $f) format-string call.
